-- Platformer — assertions about gravity, a jump, and standing on things.
--
-- Written in the relative vocabulary as always, so one suite covers every
-- console: the shelves are four cells apart everywhere, but the hero's jump is
-- a multiple of its own `speed`, which is a share of the playfield's width.
--
-- Every case opens with `press a`, because every game opens on its title
-- screen. That is one line of ceremony in exchange for the title screen
-- being part of what the suite checks rather than something it routes
-- around: a game that never reached `play` would fail every case below.

test gravity pulls the hero down
press a
play 0.33 seconds
expect player.ydirection > 0
expect player.y > 2

test the hero lands on the ground and stops falling
press a
play 4 seconds
expect player.ydirection <= 0.05
expect player.bottom <= screenheight

test jumping from the ground lifts the hero
press a
play 4 seconds
press a
play 6 ticks
expect player.ydirection < 0

-- The jump has to clear the step between one shelf and the next, or half the
-- course is scenery. Measured at the apex, which is 37 ticks after the press on
-- every console because gravity and the impulse are both in `speed`.
test a jump clears the step between shelves
press a
play 4 seconds
press a
play 0.67 seconds
expect player.bottom <= screenheight - 4

-- The bug this rule exists to stop: with the jump bound straight to the button,
-- pressing it again in mid-air renewed the impulse, and the hero climbed the sky
-- one press at a time. The second press here must do nothing at all.
test the hero cannot jump again in mid air
press a
play 4 seconds
press a
play 0.33 seconds
press a
play 2 ticks
expect player.ydirection > -1

test the hero runs to the left edge and stops
press a
hold left for 5 seconds
expect player.x = 0
expect player.xdirection = 0

-- `visible 0` is inert: not drawn, not collided with, not moved. So a coin
-- scores exactly once however long the hero stands in it.
test a collected coin is gone for good
press a
play 4 seconds
hold right for 1.5 seconds
expect score.value = 1
expect coin1.visible = 0
play 4 seconds
expect score.value = 1
